; The rule deck. Requests in from loader: a letter's code (1-26) or a card to pass on. For a letter it reads through
; the rule deck (dealt again and again, INP at gd and fwd) to the letter's section (900 + the code) and sends the section's
; rules on to rule.cq, up to and with its end (999). Any other card goes on as it is.
;
; Address Contents Label Opcode Operand Comment
  03            rq      INP   r        03-10: a request
  04                    CLA   r
  05                    SUB   00
  06                    TAC   pass
  07                    SUB   c26
  08                    TAC   sec
  09            pass    OUT   r
  10                    JMP   rq
  11            sec     CLA   r        11-26: the section, and on with it
  12                    ADD   c900
  13                    STO   h
  14            gd      INP   d
  15                    CLA   d
  16                    SUB   h
  17                    TAC   gd
  18                    SUB   00
  19                    TAC   fwd
  20                    JMP   gd
  21            fwd     INP   d
  22                    OUT   d
  23                    CLA   d
  24                    SUB   c999
  25                    TAC   fwd
  26                    JMP   rq
  30            r       DATA  0
  31            d       DATA  0
  32            h       DATA  0
  33            c26     DATA  26
  34            c900    DATA  900
  35            c999    DATA  999
